            <div xml:id="d136-a1-a6">

                <pb facs="0472" n="414" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg414"/>


                <head>Mexican Republic–National Army–General of brigade.</head>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Citizen Minister</hi>: I learn with pleasure from
                    your note of the 7th instant of the appointment of myself as governor of the
                    State of Tamaulipas, by the chief magistrate of the republic.</p>
                <p>I accept the office, but I must say that I do it because the State is in trouble
                    in every branch of its administration, physical, moral, political, and
                    military.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to express my thanks to the President for the confidence he has shown
                    for me in giving me the office.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Liberty and independence!
                            <placeName>Monterey</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1866-08-26">August 26, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>SANTIAGO TAPIA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Citizen Minister of Relations and
                            Government</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Chihuahua</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
